#75502
"Around a Small Campfire"
"The grass surrounding the campfire has been uprooted and moved away,
preventing the small flames from spreading.  Further from the fire, the grass
is flattened against the ground by those frequently gathering around its
warmth.  To the south three wagons sit in a semi-circle, blocking the view of
the plains visible in all other directions.
"
